It's all thanks to my poor starting stuff. The most useful item being
a +1 =oAccuracy, I told myself "Screw it, I'll kill myself by quaffing
fountains".
FWDYW? A blessed figurine of an Archon

I spent most of the early game engraving Elbereth while my Archon
(named Leylah) did the dirty job.
He cleared out Minetown. Before the priest got killed, I had just
enough time to buy 7 points of AC using the money from the
shopkeepers. I could then convert the altar safely and sacrifice for
Magicbane. Izchak had a magic lamp, that I used strictly as a light
source. One of the tree gave me 2 eucalyptus leaves, that I blessed
and used to "magically" call Leylah.
I stupidly ate a tengu corpse, hoping for teleport control. All I got
was teleportitis, that pissed me off for 20k turns. It also caused
some tricky situations, but the eucalyptus leaves saved me.
Mine's End had (besides the luckstone) a magic marker. I dug in a
fountain to create pools of water, blanked a few scrolls, wrote a
cursed ?oGenocide (on the second try), engraved Elbereth, put on a
Shield of Reflection, and sent in some Silver Dragons. Leylah
dispatched them easily, and I could enchant the scales to SDSM. I also
wrote a few ?o Enchant Weapon and got MB to +6.

Now that my Wizard was kicking asses in melee, I felt confident enough
to start killing things without Leylah (at this point, I was still
level 5 or 6). Sokoban gave me a BoH. I kept descending deeper in the
Dungeons of Doom. I later identified a =o Teleport Control (yeah!),
that may or may not come from Soko.
On Dlvl 16 (I think), I was striked by the vision of a 2x3 room
containing 2 wands, a fountain and a chest. Let's engrave-ID those
wands...
FWDYW? A blessed amulet of live saving
What's that? Extrinsic telepathy? Of sh**!
The wand was 0:2.
FWDYW? A blessed amulet of /life/ saving
Yeah, I just wasted a wish because of a typo. Considering that I never
made use of the =oLS, that's actually two wasted wishes.
Deeper in the dungeons, I found Maud's ghost. It was a paying
discovery: 2 magic markers and a Helmet of Brilliance. Thanks to the
former, I could enchant the latter to +5, and write a blessed ?oC.
Recharged my /oW and wished for speed boots.

From this point I had pretty much nothing to fear. Cleared the castle
(never used the /oW found there). Did the quest. Wished for another
magic marker. Polypiled the 12 pages of junk drops in the castle: got
GoD and T-Shirt. Enchanted, blessed and fooproofed everything. Got
crowned for Finger of Death. Wrote Magic Mapping. Sent in some wraiths
for level 30. After 40k turns, I had -42AC, maxed stats and all but
one intrinsics. Telepathy. Not that I murdered anything: I did not saw
a single Floating Eye corpse during the whole game (but eventually got
telepathy from a Mind Flayer).

Despite all this preparation, I excpected the end game to be very
challenging. It wasn't. Rodney isn't a worry thanks to FoD. Riders
aren't so fast and/or though that they can't be killed without getting
hit. Conflict makes everything an awful lot easier. I was even lucky
enough to start next to the right altar.
"Thoth? Did I read Thoth? Oh f*** Yeah!"
A shiver ran down my spine...


